From f73325a52d57bcadb397cd74d2a3b4a7b1e60e63 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude (Anthropic)" <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 00:41:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(oci): correct call-trace step attribution race, expose
 trace viewer on every stage
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- OciStepContext previously used a single shared AtomicReference for step
  attribution, introduced when fixing an earlier ThreadLocal thread-hop bug.
  This app has no re-entrancy guard on OCI-calling coroutines
  (viewModelScope.launch for verify/discover/fetchShapes/fetchImages/
  provisioning can genuinely overlap), so the shared reference could
  silently mislabel one call's trace entries with another call's step.

- Root cause of the original thread-hop bug: Retrofit's suspend function
  support runs via Call.enqueue(), whose callback executes on OkHttp's own
  pooled Dispatcher threads, not the calling coroutine's thread — so no
  thread-local or coroutine-context mechanism (plain ThreadLocal or
  kotlinx.coroutines asContextElement) can reach OciSigningInterceptor from
  the call site.

- Fix: OciStepContext reverts to a genuine per-thread ThreadLocal (correct,
  since it's only read synchronously at Call-creation time). New
  OciStepCallTagger (OkHttp EventListener.Factory) reads that value the
  moment OkHttpClient.newCall() fires -- synchronously, on the true calling
  thread, before any suspension -- and tags the immutable Call object
  itself, which survives the async dispatch unlike ambient thread state.
  OciSigningInterceptor now reads via OciStepCallTagger.stepFor(chain.call())
  instead of ambient state.

- OciOnboardingScreen: added a persistent 'API Call Traces' icon in the
  wizard's top bar, visible on every stage regardless of error state --
  the previous only entry points were inside OciDiagnosticsCard, gated
  behind error != null && diagnostics != null, contradicting the 'available
  at any time' requirement this feature exists to satisfy.

Tests not updated as part of this change (OciStepContextTest.kt and
OciSigningInterceptorTest.kt reference the prior design/API and will need
revision) -- deferred per instruction.
